      "title": "Make preferences more memory scope independent",
      "message": "Make preferences more memory scope independent\n\nHave preference modules and preferences be assigned a memory scope and not always default to using wmem_epan_scope() and g_ scoped memory.  This allows the preference functionality to be more reusable outside of epan.\n\nConvert structured global preference data to use wmem_epan_scope() as well\n",
      "author_name": "Michael Mann",
      "author_email": "mmann78@netscape.net",
      "authored_date": "2026-01-06T10:52:32.000-05:00",
      "committer_name": "Michael Mann",
